Aerie-Purpose: Put the Aerie sidebar view into the vertical tab strip region view, in place of the tab strip and its bottom container.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #177. VerticalTabStripRegionView is final and is also the owner of the column's slot in the
window layout, its background, its resize area and its width, so the sidebar swaps its contents
instead of replacing the class (docs/sidebar-design.md, "Native sidebar view"). While the layout is
the sidebar the constructor adds AerieSidebarView (overlay, chrome/browser/ui/views/aerie_sidebar)
to the content area and hides the bottom container. The tab strip view is still added, because
the code that reads it expects it, but it is hidden. The region says "generic container" to a
screen reader, because the sidebar view is the navigation landmark and holds the tree of tabs.

